00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:54,200
Okay.

247
00:15:56,910 --> 00:16:00,660
You don't have to be awake To be my man

248
00:16:02,830 --> 00:16:07,880
Long as you have brain waves I'll be there to hold your hand

249
00:16:09,170 --> 00:16:11,710
Though we just met the other day

250
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:15,180
There's something I have got to say

251
00:16:16,260 --> 00:16:19,310
Okay, thank you very much. I'm gonna take a short break.

252
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:25,230
Okay, that was Phoebe Buffay, everybody. Whoo!

253
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:29,190
- What the hell was that?     - Phoebe just started...

254
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:32,990
I believe I was talking to Joey. All right, there, mother-kisser?

255
00:16:38,370 --> 00:16:40,120
"Mother-kisser."

256
00:16:41,450 --> 00:16:42,790
I'll shut up.

257
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:45,580
Chandler, can I say something? I know you're still mad at me.

258
00:16:45,750 --> 00:16:48,960
I just wanna say that there were two people there that night, okay?

259
00:16:49,130 --> 00:16:52,050
- There were two sets of lips.     - Yes, well, I expect this from her.

260
00:16:52,210 --> 00:16:54,970
Okay? She's always been a Freudian nightmare.

261
00:16:55,130 --> 00:16:58,340
Okay, but if she always behaves like this, why don't you say something?

262
00:16:58,510 --> 00:17:01,390
Because it's complicated. It's complex.

263
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,220
Hey, you kissed my mom.

264
00:17:07,190 --> 00:17:09,440
We're rehearsing a Greek play.

265
00:17:10,770 --> 00:17:12,570
- That's funny. We done now?     - No.

266
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:15,990
Okay, you mean you're not gonna talk to her, tell her how you feel?

267
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:19,450
That would be a no. Just because you played tonsil tennis with my mom...

268
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:22,830
...doesn't mean you know her, all right? Trust me, you can't talk to her.

269
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,370
Okay. "You can't"? Or you can't?

270
00:17:26,620 --> 00:17:30,960
Okay, that's my finger. Okay, that's my knee.

271
00:17:31,130 --> 00:17:32,920
Still doing the play.

272
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:42,760
All right, what did you do with him?

273
00:17:47,020 --> 00:17:48,940
- You're awake.     - Look at you.

274
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:50,100
How do you feel?

275
00:17:50,270 --> 00:17:53,360
Uh, a little woozy, but basically okay.

276
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:55,570
Gosh, you look good.

277
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:57,530
I feel good.

278
00:17:58,410 --> 00:17:59,910
Who are you?

279
00:18:00,070 --> 00:18:01,740
- Sorry.     - I'm Phoebe Buffay.

280
00:18:01,910 --> 00:18:04,490
I'm Monica Geller. I've been taking care of you.

281
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:05,660
We both have.

282
00:18:05,830 --> 00:18:08,830
- So the Etch A Sketch is from you guys?     - Actually, it's just from me.

283
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,920
- Yeah, I got you the foot massager.     - Know who shaved you? That was me.

284
00:18:12,090 --> 00:18:15,000
- I read to you.     - I sang. Ha.

285
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:17,970
Well, thanks.

286
00:18:18,130 --> 00:18:20,380
- Oh, my pleasure.     - You're welcome.

287
00:18:20,550 --> 00:18:23,510
So I guess I'll see you around.

288
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:26,350
What? That's it?

289
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:28,600
"See you around"?

290
00:18:28,770 --> 00:18:32,060
- Well, what do you want me to say?     - Well, I don't know.

291
00:18:32,230 --> 00:18:33,560
Maybe, uh:

292
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:35,110
"That was nice.

293
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,730
It meant something to me.

294
00:18:37,990 --> 00:18:39,860
I'll call you."

295
00:18:40,570 --> 00:18:44,030
- All right. I'll call you.     - I don't think you mean that.

296
00:18:47,290 --> 00:18:49,370
This is so typical.

297
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:50,670
You know, we give...

298
00:18:50,830 --> 00:18:52,290
...and we give...

299
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:54,000
...and we give.

300
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:56,460
And then we just get nothing back.

301
00:18:56,630 --> 00:19:00,470
And then one day, it's just, you know, you wake up and "See you around."

302
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:04,550
Let's go, Phoebe.

303
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:08,890
You know what? We thought you were different.

304
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:11,350
But I guess it was just the coma.

305
00:19:16,230 --> 00:19:17,610
The car's running downstairs.

306
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:20,240
I wanted to drop off these copies of my book for your friends.

307
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:25,580
- Anything you want from Lisbon?     - No, just knowing you're there is enough.

308
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:29,830
All right. Well, be good. I love you.

309
00:19:32,540 --> 00:19:34,130
You kissed my best Ross.

310
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:38,550
Or something to that effect.

311
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:41,840
Okay.

312
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:47,640
Look, it was stupid.

313
00:19:47,810 --> 00:19:50,180
- Really stupid.     - Really stupid.

314
00:19:52,350 --> 00:19:54,690
And I don't even know how it happened.

315
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:58,730
I'm sorry, honey. I promise it will never happen again.

316
00:20:00,690 --> 00:20:03,030
- Are we okay now?     - Yeah.

317
00:20:03,780 --> 00:20:06,490
No. No.

318
00:20:10,290 --> 00:20:12,960
Ah, the forbidden love of a man and his door.

319
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:14,370
Shh.

320
00:20:15,170 --> 00:20:18,460
He did it. He told her off. And not just about the kiss, about everything.

321
00:20:18,630 --> 00:20:19,670
- You're kidding?     - No.

322
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:22,510
He said, "When are you gonna grow up and start being a mom?"

323
00:20:22,670 --> 00:20:24,760
- Wow.     - Wait, then she came back with:

324
00:20:24,970 --> 00:20:29,470
"The question is, when are you gonna grow up and realize I have a bomb?"

325
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,100
Okay, wait. Are you sure she didn't say:

326
00:20:33,270 --> 00:20:37,100
"When are you gonna grow up and realize I am your mom?"

327
00:20:40,730 --> 00:20:42,820
- That makes more sense.     - You think?

328
00:20:42,990 --> 00:20:44,530
Yeah.

329
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:46,780
So, what's going on now?

330
00:20:46,950 --> 00:20:49,990
I don't know. I've been standing here spelling it out for you.

331
00:20:52,410 --> 00:20:54,330
I don't hear anything. Wait, wait, wait.

332
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:55,710
What do you see?

333
00:20:55,870 --> 00:20:58,290
It's hard to tell. They're so tiny and upside down.

334
00:20:58,460 --> 00:20:59,790
Wait, wait, wait.

335
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:03,380
They're walking away. They're walking away.

336
00:21:03,550 --> 00:21:06,970
No, they're not. They're coming right at us. Run, run!

337
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:10,810
You okay, kiddo?

338
00:21:10,970 --> 00:21:14,230
- Yeah, I'm okay.     - All right. You be good.

339
00:21:14,390 --> 00:21:16,140
Drive safe.

340
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:20,770
- Mrs. Bing.     - Mr. Geller.

341
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:27,200
Hey.

342
00:21:29,120 --> 00:21:30,620
You mean that?

343
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:33,450
Yeah, why not?

344
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:36,870
- So I told her.     - Oh.

345
00:21:37,580 --> 00:21:39,580
- How did it go?     - Awful. Awful.

346
00:21:39,750 --> 00:21:41,670
Couldn't have gone worse.

347
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:45,260
- Well, how do you feel?     - Pretty good.

348
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:48,840
I told her.

349
00:21:49,010 --> 00:21:51,010
Well, see?

350
00:21:51,180 --> 00:21:55,350
So maybe it wasn't such a bad idea, you know, me kissing your mom, huh?

351
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:58,020
But we don't have to go down that road.

352
00:22:04,690 --> 00:22:06,650
Now, this is just the first chapter...

353
00:22:06,820 --> 00:22:11,950
...and I want your absolute honest opinion. Okay?

354
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:16,830
Oh, and on page two, he's not reaching for her "heaving beasts."

355
00:22:17,870 --> 00:22:18,960
What's a "niffle"?

356
00:22:19,210 --> 00:22:22,130
You can usually find them on the heaving beasts.

357
00:22:24,250 --> 00:22:26,510
All right, all right, so I'm not a great typist.

358
00:22:26,670 --> 00:22:30,720
Wait, did you get to the part about his "huge, throbbing pens"?

359
00:22:31,550 --> 00:22:34,810
Tell you, you don't wanna be around when he starts writing with those.

360
00:22:36,020 --> 00:22:38,100
- All right, that's it. Give them back.     - No.

